  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Work is equal to area under <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> graph (when P is plotted along y-axis). As area under graph 3 is maximum and area under graph 1 is minimum, so <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is maximum and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is minimum.<br />So <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0091_cd3521eed801.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 131px;\" />"
  }
